Falsifies `universally_unique_identifier::verification::stamping_reserves_six_bits_and_keeps_the_other_hundred_and_twenty_two`.

The defect: `v4_from_random` clears one bit too many in the variant byte (`0x1f` for `0x3f`). The
printed form still says variant `10`, so every sample looks right, and the stamp quietly discards a
bit of the caller's entropy.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(stamped[8] & 0x3f, raw[8] & 0x3f)`.

diff --git a/crates/universally_unique_identifier/src/lib.rs b/crates/universally_unique_identifier/src/lib.rs
index 09fc48f4c..8a5695685 100644
--- a/crates/universally_unique_identifier/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/universally_unique_identifier/src/lib.rs
@@ -107,3 +107,3 @@ impl Uuid {
         bytes[6] = (bytes[6] & 0x0f) | 0x40;
-        bytes[8] = (bytes[8] & 0x3f) | 0x80;
+        bytes[8] = (bytes[8] & 0x1f) | 0x80;
         Uuid(bytes)
